  font-size: 0.9em;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
  /* Rows off-screen skip style, layout and paint until scrolled near. This is
     what makes a whole-sheet table (tableRenderAllRows) affordable: with
     3,240 rows the browser's own work — not our JS — was ~1 s per re-sort and
     every scroll stuttered. Find-in-page still searches the skipped content and
     reveals the hit. The intrinsic size is the measured single-line row height;
     'auto' lets the browser remember a row's real height once laid out. */
